# f1 = turn. The program only reckons with `held`, so the arm of the read that finds a list of fractions takes NaN for a hole. The store into another row stands between the two products: the arms of the one read
# (a list, a view, by name) meet in a parameter in front of the second product, which asks the parameter whether it is a number to choose its form: NaN goes one way, undefined the other, and both give NaN.
# The check of the form of the code took that test for a user that tells NaN from undefined, and a right build stopped (`walk` verifies what it prints).
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetArrayElement {{*}}readsHoleAsNaN
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=number
